# XSPEC local models (GradusXSPEC)

Official references:
- [Appendix C: Adding Models to XSPEC](https://heasarc.gsfc.nasa.gov/docs/software/xspec/manual/XSappendixLocal.html)
- [OGIP 92-009 table model format memo (PDF)](https://heasarc.gsfc.nasa.gov/FTP/caldb/docs/memos/ogip_92_009/ogip_92_009.pdf)
- [Gradus.jl codebase](https://codeberg.org/astro-group/Gradus.jl)
- [Gradus.jl documentation](https://astro-group.codeberg.page/Gradus.jl/dev/)

## XSPEC concepts

- **`model.dat`**: describes the model name, parameters, and the wrapper function XSPEC calls.
- **`initpackage`**: prepares and compiles a local model library from `model.dat` and component source files.
- **`hmake`**: builds the library using the `Makefile` created by `initpackage`.
- **`lmod`**: loads the built library into a running XSPEC session.
- **Table models**: use OGIP table files. The canonical format details are in OGIP 92-009; use this when reading table-model content from files or when mapping table columns/extensions to model behavior.

Function names in `model.dat` use a language prefix (e.g. `c_gradusjulia` for C). The prefix appears only in `model.dat`; the C source defines `gradusjulia`.

## GradusXSPEC build workflow

1. **Julia library** (repo root): `./build-julia.sh`  
   Produces `build/lib/libGradusXSPEC.{dylib,so}` and writes `model.dat`.

2. **XSPEC package** (repo root, with `HEADAS` set):
   ```sh
   ./build-xspec.sh
   ```

   Or manually: `./clean-xspec-package.sh`, `initpackage <model> model.dat .`, `./patch-xspec-makefile.sh`, `hmake`. Use `./build-xspec.sh --full` for a full clean rebuild.

3. **Load in XSPEC**: `lmod gradusxspec .` then `model gradus_lamp_ss` or `model gradus_lamp_thin`

## Repo-specific: Makefile patching

`initpackage` generates a fresh `Makefile` that does not link against GradusXSPEC or Julia. Always run `./patch-xspec-makefile.sh` after `initpackage` (idempotent). It inserts into `HD_SHLIB_LIBS` after `-lXS`:

- `-Wl,-rpath,${PWD}/build/lib`
- `-Wl,-rpath,${PWD}/build/lib/julia`
- `-L${PWD}/build/lib`
- `-lGradusXSPEC`

Do not use line-number-based patches; prefer the script.

## Upstream sync notes

When implementing GradusXSPEC model logic against upstream Gradus:

1. Start with the [Gradus.jl documentation](https://astro-group.codeberg.page/Gradus.jl/dev/) to choose the right APIs and physical-model concepts.
2. Confirm exact signatures, kwargs, and defaults in the [Gradus.jl source](https://codeberg.org/astro-group/Gradus.jl) before coding.
3. If docs and source disagree, follow source-of-truth behavior from the codebase and note the mismatch in your PR/commit notes.

## Key files

| File | Role |
|------|------|
| `src/model_definition.jl` | Model names, parameters, `model.dat` generation |
| `src/model_runtime.jl` | Per-model grids, caches, spectrum evaluation |
| `src/GradusXSPEC.jl` | `@ccallable` entry points for each XSPEC model |
| `gradusxspec.c` | C wrappers (`graduslampsjulia`, `graduslampthinjulia`) — initializes Julia |
| `build-julia.sh` | Julia library build + `model.dat` generation |
| `build-xspec.sh` | XSPEC package wrapper (clean → initpackage → patch → hmake) |
| `clean-xspec-package.sh` | Remove stale `lpack_<model>.*` before re-running `initpackage` |
| `patch-xspec-makefile.sh` | Insert GradusXSPEC link flags into the XSPEC `Makefile` |
| `model.dat` | XSPEC model definition (regenerated by `build_lib.jl`) |

After changing Julia code, rebuild with `./build-julia.sh` then `./build-xspec.sh` (or `hmake` if only the Makefile is already patched).
